It's a cool idea. Another idea I was thinking of would be randomised
Sokoban. There do exist some Sokoban level generating algorithms, it
shouldn't be too hard to tweak one of them to work in Nethack. You'd
need some alteration so that the endpoints for the boulders were always
out of the "boulder map" - then you could just do them in a line, and
obviously space for the player to emerge, but it shouldn't be too
tricky.

That would keep the existing Sokoban as part of Nethack, but it would
prevent it from turning into the boredom it is now - most experienced
players can do it by heart... which is not really the point! It's
*meant* to be a puzzle.

Another option would be a maze (generated using a different algorithm
to Gehennom's, for the sake of sanity!) that resists permanent
lighting, and is magicmapping/clairvoyance proof, as well as no
teleport.

Just thoughts.

